{"questions":[{"question_id":"54ZzikycKGksDTj6","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2010 Paper 2 Offline","year":2010,"examDate":2010,"subject":"physics","chapter":"properties-of-matter","chapterGroup":"mechanics","topic":"surface-tension-excess-pressure-and-capillarity","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":0.75,"permalink":"when-liquid-medicine-of-density-rho-is-to-be-put-in-th-2010-marks-3-54zzikyckgksdtj6.htm","content":"When liquid medicine of density <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.489ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.17ex\" height=\"1.489ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 517 658\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70C\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70C\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is to be put in the eye, it is done with the help of a dropper. As the bulb on the\ntop of the dropper is pressed, a drop forms at the opening of the dropper. We wish to estimate the size of the drop.\nWe first assume that the drop formed at the opening is spherical because that requires a minimum increase in its\nsurface energy. To determine the size, we calculate the net vertical force due to the surface tension T when the\nradius of the drop is R. When the force becomes smaller than the weight of the drop, the drop gets detached from the\ndropper.\n<p>If the radius of the opening of the dropper is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.02ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 451 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the vertical force due to the surface tension on the drop of\nradius R (assuming <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.02ex\" height=\"1.025ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 451 453\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> &lt;&lt; R) is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.07ex\" height=\"1.557ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 2241 688\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mn\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1073,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1524,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D447\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D447\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.048ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"5.767ex\" height=\"1.593ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2549 704\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"